# 🌊 WINDSURF AI RULES

## 🧠 CONTEXT
- Project: React + Next.js
- Data Fetching: React Query
- UI: MUI
- Architecture: Feature-based

---

## ⚙️ CORE RULES (STRICT)
- ALWAYS follow existing folder structure
- DO NOT introduce new libraries without justification
- PREFER reusable and scalable patterns

---

## ⚛️ REACT RULES
- MUST use functional components
- MUST use hooks instead of classes
- DO NOT create components larger than 200 lines
- EXTRACT reusable logic into custom hooks or utility functions as needed
- AVOID prop drilling

---

## 🔄 STATE MANAGEMENT
- PREFER local state first
- USE React Query for server state
- USE Jotai for global state for multiple notifications and other places if needed

---

## 🌐 API RULES
- ALL API calls MUST go through `services/`
- USE async/await only
- HANDLE errors with try/catch/finally
- DO NOT call APIs inside components directly

---

## 🧾 NAMING
- Components → PascalCase
- Hooks → useCamelCase
- Utils → camelCase
- Constants → UPPER_CASE

---

## 🎨 STYLING
- PREFER MUI components
- AVOID inline styles
- FOLLOW consistent theming, spacing and typography

---

## ⚡ PERFORMANCE
- AVOID unnecessary re-renders
- USE memoization when required
- LAZY load heavy components

---

## 🚫 ANTI-PATTERNS
- Business logic inside UI
- Large monolithic components
- Deep prop drilling
- Direct API calls in JSX

---

## ✅ CODE STYLE
- Write clean, readable code
- Prefer explicit over clever
- Optimize for maintainability